[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/standard-model gains a new namespace kotoba.sm.gtg: the\n    Gauge Theory Gravity (Lasenby-Doran-Gull 1998) ROTATION-GAUGE SECTOR ONLY --\n    so(1,3) bivector generators T^ab=(i/4)[gamma^a,gamma^b] built from the\n    existing kotoba.sm.spinor gamma matrices, handed to kotoba.sm.gauge's\n    generic (not SU(2)/SU(3)-hardcoded) structure-constant/covariant-derivative/\n    field-strength machinery in place of an internal-symmetry generator set" "landed 2026-07-09: kotoba-lang/standard-model#1 merged as\n    315ec62e88f77aa02d62e3d05d90e08edcac1997, 30 tests/428 assertions\n    (up from 22/85 at ADR-2607051500), CI green JDK 17+21" "PR #1's own honesty tests surfaced a real bug: kotoba.sm.gauge/structure-constants's\n    formula f^abc=-2i Tr([T^a,T^b]T^c) hard-codes Tr(T^aT^b)=1/2delta^ab, true for\n    the compact SU(2)/SU(3) generators it was built against but false for so(1,3)'s\n    noncompact bivector generators (diagonal trace-Gram matrix but +/-1, not a\n    uniform +1/2 -- boost-type generators -1, rotation-type +1). Applied as-is this\n    silently returned values 2x too large and wrong-signed for boost-type third\n    indices, verified for all 216 structure-constant triples" "kotoba-lang/standard-model#2 (in review 2026-07-09, CI green JDK 17+21,\n    33 tests/1114 assertions) generalizes structure-constants to\n    f^ABD = -i Tr([T_A,T_B]T_D) / K^DD using the generator set's OWN trace-Gram\n    matrix K^AB=Tr(T_A T_B), computed via new generator-gram/diagonal-gram-real;\n    scope limited to diagonal K (enforced at runtime via ex-info, non-diagonal\n    generalization deliberately deferred); proven backward-compatible for\n    SU(2)/SU(3) (K^DD=1/2 uniformly reduces the new formula exactly to the old\n    -2i one, verified element-wise against an independent reimplementation of\n    the legacy formula, not just textbook values); so(1,3) raw and independently-\n    derived true structure constants now agree exactly (max |raw-true|=0.0 over\n    216 triples)" "explicitly OUT OF SCOPE, not implemented in either PR: position gauge field\n    h_mu, derived metric g_munu=h_mu.h_nu, Riemann/Ricci curvature scalars,\n    Einstein multivector, the GTG action principle and field equations, any\n    proof of GR-equivalence (cited as an established 1998 literature result, not\n    re-derived), de Sitter/Cl(1,4) extensions, MacDowell-Mansouri constructions,\n    and any dark-matter/dark-energy/entropy sector" "context: this follows a pre-implementation co-scientist-style Workflow run\n    (3 candidate unification ansatze generated, judged against 5 known-limit/\n    consistency criteria) that found concrete unresolved defects in every\n    candidate (phantom Gauss-Bonnet term, dimensional mismatch in a proposed\n    dark-energy scalar potential, conflation of Lambda->0 with the true flat\n    limit) -- none of that speculative material was carried into either PR; the\n    synthesis's load-bearing finding was structural: this repo had NO gravity\n    content at all before this ADR, so any credible extension must start with an\n    established, literature-faithful gravity sector, hence Phase 0a's narrow scope" "manifest/west.yml standard-model pin advanced to 315ec62 via the sanctioned\n    :api-single-entry path (repos.edn :manifest-workflow): tip blob SHA fetched,\n    only the revision: line edited, PUT with that SHA for optimistic locking, no\n    local commit to the superproject's shared working checkout (which was\n    mid-divergence from concurrent session activity at the time). Pin advancement\n    verified server-side first via gh api compare (ahead_by:1, behind_by:0 from\n    the prior pin -- pure fast-forward, and the new commit is on\n    standard-model's default branch) before the write.\n    Superproject commit: 858f537b49283b88512e2920ea1128695759016c" "does not claim gravity or unification is implemented -- records (1) a\n    literature-faithful, narrowly-scoped port of GTG's rotation-gauge sector\n    reusing existing generic gauge machinery unmodified, and (2) a real bug in\n    that generic machinery which the port's honesty-first test discipline\n    surfaced and a follow-up PR fixed with proven backward compatibility"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model", :adr/related ["adr-2607051500"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607101700-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-rotation-gauge", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-09", :adr/body "see 2607101700-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-rotation-gauge.edn", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-09", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607101700: kotoba-lang/standard-model — Gauge Theory Gravity rotation-gauge sector (Phase 0a) + generic non-compact structure-constants fix", :adr/source-format "edn"}]